  user_input {
    user_response: "Vastaa suomen kielell\303\244 (fi), arvioi ideani: \"Act as the product architect, UX lead and implementation engineer for AOS Product v0.1. Read the attached file \"AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23.md\" fully and treat it as the authoritative product handoff, subject to the security/ownership rules it describes.\n\nGoal: Build a runnable, mobile-first AOS Custom Skins PWA that demonstrates ONE governed AOS Engine serving MANY experiences under ONE account with N authorized devices. Include: a welcoming AI prompt screen, immediately useful default skins, Field Service and Driver demos, Skin Library, schema-validated widgets, stateful customization with Save/Cancel, and a transparent mock-or-live intent -> proposal -> human approval workflow.\n\nStart with a brief verified-vs-assumed matrix and technical approach, then create working code and run the tests available in your environment. Evaluate reusable open-source AI UIs and the existing PWA starter before choosing a frontend foundation. Respect existing AOS, DMS, Messaging, mcp-connector and LocalAI authority boundaries. Never claim access to local repos or live integrations unless actually verified. Never create charges, deploy, relax authorization, call live mutation APIs, or push code without specific permission.\n\nDeliver runnable artifacts, instructions, responsive demonstration, exact test results and a prioritized v0.2 gap list. Build a small functional vertical slice rather than a static mockup or theoretical architecture document.  \"\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "Vastaa suomen kielell\303\244 (fi), arvioi ideani: \"Act as the product architect, UX lead and implementation engineer for AOS Product v0.1. Read the attached file \"AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23.md\" fully and treat it as the authoritative product handoff, subject to the security/ownership rules it describes.\n\nGoal: Build a runnable, mobile-first AOS Custom Skins PWA that demonstrates ONE governed AOS Engine serving MANY experiences under ONE account with N authorized devices. Include: a welcoming AI prompt screen, immediately useful default skins, Field Service and Driver demos, Skin Library, schema-validated widgets, stateful customization with Save/Cancel, and a transparent mock-or-live intent -> proposal -> human approval workflow.\n\nStart with a brief verified-vs-assumed matrix and technical approach, then create working code and run the tests available in your environment. Evaluate reusable open-source AI UIs and the existing PWA starter before choosing a frontend foundation. Respect existing AOS, DMS, Messaging, mcp-connector and LocalAI authority boundaries. Never claim access to local repos or live integrations unless actually verified. Never create charges, deploy, relax authorization, call live mutation APIs, or push code without specific permission.\n\nDeliver runnable artifacts, instructions, responsive demonstration, exact test results and a prioritized v0.2 gap list. Build a small functional vertical slice rather than a static mockup or theoretical architecture document.  \"\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
    media {
      mime_type: "text/markdown"
      uri: "/public/assets/aistudio/AOS_Product_V0.1_Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23_ee15dce9.md"
    }
  }
}
