    response: "Arvioin AOS Product v0.1 -tuotekonseptin ja build-briefin eritt\303\244in vahvaksi, ammattimaiseksi ja tuotantokelpoiseksi handoff-m\303\244\303\244rittelyksi.\n\n### Idean ja arkkitehtuurin arviointi\n\n1. **Ydinlupaus (\"One Account, N Devices, Many Experiences\") osuu suoraan teko\303\244lysovellusten kipupisteeseen:** Useimmat nykyratkaisut joko pystytt\303\244v\303\244t jokaiseen toimialaan erillisen raskaan SaaS-siilon tai tarjoavat geneerisen chatbotin, joka ei tee mit\303\244\303\244n konkreettista. AOS:n arkkitehtuuri pit\303\244\303\244 tilinhallinnan, kontekstin, valtuutukset ja toimintamoottorin yhten\303\244isen\303\244, samalla kun k\303\244ytt\303\244j\303\244kokemus (Skin) mukautuu t\303\244ysin kohderyhm\303\244n (kuten kentt\303\244ty\303\266ntekij\303\244n tai kuljettajan) sanastoon ja ty\303\266nkulkuun.\n2. **Hallittu suoritussykli (Human-directed AI):** *Intent \342\206\222 Interpretation \342\206\222 Proposal \342\206\222 Human Approval \342\206\222 Bounded Execution* -malli on elint\303\244rke\303\244 yritysk\303\244ytt\303\244jille. Reaalimaailman toimenpiteit\303\244 ei koskaan tapahdu arvaamalla, vaan ehdotus on aina tarkastettavissa ja hyv\303\244ksytt\303\244viss\303\244 ennen ajoa.\n3. **Rehellinen tila ja rajapintakuri:** Tiukka jako oikeaan ja simuloituun dataan (`mock/demo` vs `live`) sek\303\244 kielto valheelliselle valmiudelle luo luotettavan pohjan v0.1:n validoinnille.\n\nToteutussuunnitelman tarkentamiseksi ja k\303\244ytt\303\266kokemuksen hienos\303\244\303\244t\303\244miseksi vahvistetaan muutama keskeinen linjaus:"
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Instructions**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt and instructions. My primary focus is understanding the user\'s request: I need to act as a multifaceted expert for a new product, AOS Product v0.1. I\'m carefully reviewing the context provided, specifically the attached file \"AOS_Product_V0.1_\", to fully grasp the product\'s scope and the required deliverables. This is the foundation upon which I\'ll build my responses.\n\n\n**Defining the Deliverables**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the core deliverables outlined in \"Gemini_Build_Brief_2026-10-23.md,\" treating it as the definitive product blueprint. I\'m focusing on the specifications for the AOS Custom Skins PWA, and how to create a mobile-first, governed AOS engine that can handle multiple experiences. The features are numerous, and include AI prompts, default skins, demos, a skin library, schema-validated widgets, customization with save/cancel, and an approval workflow. I am currently considering the \"AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START\" instructions, too.\n\n\n**Clarifying Initial Directions**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the \"AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START\" directives, specifically the call for clarification when design aspects are unclear. I will use the ask_question tool, formulating 2-4 multiple-choice questions to hone in on brand identity, visual aesthetics, or key features. My focus will be concise options, using the (Recommended) prefix where appropriate. I\'ll yield immediately after, keeping any text response minimal, and will not immediately output a plan.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Concept**\n\nI\'m now assessing the Finnish product concept and brief. I need to formulate 2-3 clarification questions using the `ask_question` tool. I must adhere to the formatting guidelines strictly: plain text only, short questions, concise options, and no markdown. My focus will be on key design/architectural decisions. I\'ll translate the questions to Finnish, and consider these for my questions: \"Painotus ja ensisijainen k\303\244ytt\303\266liittym\303\244tyyli\", \"Rakennettavuus ja skaalautuvuus\", and \"Tavoiteltu k\303\244ytt\303\244j\303\244kokemus\". I\'ll use `ask_question` with 3 key clarifying questions on design/architectural tradeoffs to get feedback before the implementation plan.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Design Choices**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the key architectural and design decisions for the product. Specifically, I\'m considering the core questions for feedback before moving on. I have a more in-depth Finnish evaluation of the brief and its value: \"One Account, N Devices, Many Experiences\" resolves typical AI application fragmentation by separating the AOS Engine and Skins. The framework of execution and \"Human Intent -> Interpretation -> Proposal -> Human Approval\" will be essential. I will focus on the UI foundation, engine connection mode, and device presentation with multi-device support, using the `ask_question` tool.\n\n\n"
